[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   Step 086 -- slip-physics discriminator: where in the orbit does
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   the anomaly act?
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   The inner-shell profile (step 076) shows the in-cap rotation excess
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   is already fully developed at the innermost probed shell of 8 AU --
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   inside the region where the comet is observed and the reconstruction
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   residual is generated.  That leaves a discriminating question the
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   radial profile alone cannot answer: is the slip a temporal offset
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   imprinted during the observed arc, a temporal offset imprinted at a
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   distant boundary crossing, or a fixed angular displacement?
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   For near-parabolic comets the three readings predict different
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   power-law scalings of the measured rotation with perihelion
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   distance q (h ~ q^{1/2}):
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   angular systematic   d_theta ~ q^0      (a fixed apsidal error:
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   zonal catalogue error or
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   directional fit bias)
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   boundary time slip   d_theta = dtau*h/r_b^2 ~ q^{+0.5}
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   (fixed proper-time offset at a ~250 AU
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   crossing; more angular
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   momentum h sweeps more
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   angle per unit time slip)
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   arc-epoch time slip  d_theta = omega_dot_arc * dtau ~ q^{-1.5}
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   (fixed time offset absorbed by the fit at
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   the observed-arc epoch;
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   the perihelion sweep rate
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   dominates and scales as
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   q^{-3/2})
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   Equivalently, on the boundary-normalized time slip
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   dtau = d_theta * r_b^2 / h the predictions are
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   angular    slope(dtau ~ q) = -0.5
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   boundary   slope            =  0
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   arc-epoch  slope            = -2.0
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   One dataset, one slope measurement on each of two normalizations,
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   three separated model points: (0, -0.5), (+0.5, 0), (-1.5, -2).
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   The out-of-cap cohort supplies the control -- a sky- or
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   catalogue-wide systematic would carry its scaling into both caps;
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   a boundary mechanism acts only on the crossing population.
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   Data: per-comet catalogue rotations drot_cat and boundary-
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   normalized slips dtau_cat from step_b30_proper_time_slip.csv
[2026-09-21 14:54:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 086]   (CODE n=131, Warsaw n=98; theta vs the transit axis).
